<graph edgedefault="directed"><node id="Paper:regolith">
  <data key="d0">Statistical Analysis and Modeling of the 3D Morphology and Texture of Lunar Regolith Simulants</data>
  <data key="d1">Document</data>
  <data key="d2">The paper uses 3D X-ray micro-CT data and multivariate statistical/parametric modeling to quantify size and shape descriptor distributions for lunar regolith particles and seven mare/highlands simulants, finding large morphological differences among simulants and versus lunar regolith and motivating improved simulants or statistically representative digital models for simulation-based studies of morphology-driven mechanical behavior relevant to ISRU. (regolith.pdf p.1, p.2)</data>
  <data key="d3">regolith.pdf</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d5">regolith.pdf</data>
  <data key="d6">1.0</data>
  <data key="d7">regolith</data>
</node>
